  "name": "dependency-risk-rating",
  "description": "Rates how risky an npm dependency version bump is and whether it is safe to merge, whoever opened it — Dependabot, Renovate, a Fullsend agent, or a person. Takes a pull request, a package.json / yarn.lock / package-lock.json change including a lockfile-only diff, or a single bump named as \"lodash 4.17.20 -> 4.17.21\". Produces a per-package table, a LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH band with a 0-100 score, a merge recommendation, and the data gaps behind it, from npm registry metadata, OSV vulnerabilities, weekly downloads, OpenSSF Scorecard, @backstage/* release-manifest alignment, and Backstage-ecosystem support levels. Use for \"rate this dependency bump\", \"how risky is this update\", \"is this bump safe to merge\", or a queue of pending version-bump pull requests. Works from the manifest and lockfile delta plus registry data.",
